VERIFIED    DV09-02 [Onkelos Deut 9:7; Onkelos Deut 9:8; Onkelos Deut 9:9; Onkelos Deut 9:10; Onkelos Deut 9:11; Onkelos Deut 9:12; Onkelos Deut 9:13; Onkelos Deut 9:14; Sifrei Devarim 14:1; Sifrei Devarim 27:2; Sifrei Devarim 306:25; Sifrei Devarim 342:1] THE CALF RETOLD, THE FIRST FORTY DAYS: REMEMBER, DO NOT FORGET, HOW YOU PROVOKED THE LORD IN THE WILDERNESS — FROM THE DAY YOU WENT OUT OF EGYPT UNTIL YOU CAME TO THIS PLACE YOU HAVE BEEN REBELLIOUS; AT HOREB YOU PROVOKED HIM AND HE WAS ANGRY, TO DESTROY YOU; WHEN I WENT UP TO RECEIVE THE TABLETS OF STONE, THE TABLETS OF THE COVENANT, I STAYED FORTY DAYS AND FORTY NIGHTS WITHOUT BREAD OR WATER; THE LORD GAVE ME THE TWO TABLETS WRITTEN WITH THE FINGER OF GOD, ON THEM ALL THE WORDS SPOKEN FROM THE MIDST OF THE FIRE ON THE DAY OF THE ASSEMBLY; AT THE END OF FORTY DAYS HE GAVE THEM AND SAID: ARISE, GO DOWN QUICKLY, YOUR PEOPLE HAVE CORRUPTED, THEY HAVE MADE A MOLTEN IMAGE; I HAVE SEEN THIS PEOPLE, A STIFF-NECKED PEOPLE — LET ME ALONE AND I WILL DESTROY THEM AND BLOT OUT THEIR NAME, AND MAKE OF YOU A NATION MIGHTIER AND MORE NUMEROUS THAN THEY. 'Provoke' the hiphil 9:7, 8, 22 — the Torah's three, all this chapter's; 'and the LORD was angry' 1:37, 4:21, 9:8, 9:20 — the book's four; 'the tablets of the covenant' 9:9, 9:11, 9:15 — the Bible's three; 'tablets' in three spellings, two inside 9:11; 'forty days and forty nights' [40, 40] at 9:9, 9:11 (nine seats in the Bible); 'the covenant which the LORD cut with you' Exodus 24:8's clause; 'written with the finger of God' Exodus 31:18 and 9:10 alone; 'the day of the assembly' 9:10, 10:4, 18:16; 9:12 against Exodus 32:8 nine tokens, 9:13 against 32:9 ELEVEN OF THIRTEEN — God's word quoted whole but for 'to me, saying'; 'let Me alone' one seat; the offer's third form (Exodus 32:10; Numbers 14:12; 9:14); the register switches inside 9:7. The Sifrei 14:1 and 306:25: the forty days Moses' suffering for the Torah (with Exodus 34:28 — the English's 'Ex.36:28' a slip); 27:2: 'let Me